{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters","id":706070,"title":"New Wizened: Inspiration characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-17T19:28:54-07:00","id":706070,"title":"New Wizened: Inspiration characters?","content":"I don't think I've made it a secret that I'm not particularly enthusiastic about the new aesthetic they've given the Wizened, with the perceived emphasis on pseudo-technological self-reconstruction. I've recently realized that part of the issue is that I have trouble seeing that sort of aesthetic as part of the fairy-tale thematic which Lost is based on. <br /> <br /> That is, however, something which can be helped. Can anyone point out to me fairy-story characters which would suit the new Wizened aesthetic? I say fairy-story rather than fairy-tale because I want to include options like the Tin Woodsman (who I admit probably falls closest to this aesthetic, to my knowledge) but I *do* want to focus on stories with thematics that're strongly Lost - otherworlds, stolen children, Fair Folk, and the like.<br /> <br /> So - who can people point to and say &quot;That's a Wizened?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T21:46:53-07:00","id":708128,"title":"","content":"Dwarves. Goblins. Kobolds.<br /> <br /> Sayaka Miki, to some extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T23:01:19-07:00","id":708192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708128#post708128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dwarves. Goblins. Kobolds..</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see them as Grimms in 2ED paradigm, but not Wizened as portrayed in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-wizened/\" target=\"_blank\">their</a> and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Kiths</a> spoilers. Wizined are mention to exchange body parts for their <i>Art</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wizened 2ED spoiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Appearance</b>: You\u2019ll know the Wizened by his stiff joints and muttering. He talks to himself about high concepts of his craft that you can\u2019t possibly understand. He caries the aire of the dysfunctional genius who so very close to solve a Millennial Prize Problem, but can\u2019t remember to tie his shoes. She is a violinist so perfect in her performance that must be reminded to stop practicing when her fingers start to bleed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To the Changeling, she is incomplete, where parts of herself are replaced with parts of her craft. She is a surgeon without fingers or face, both of which having been replaced with obsidian scalpels and a mask respectively. He is a woodsman of tin and wood, limbs replaced when the axe slipped. She\u2019s a dancer with feet made of silk and leather, stuffed pointe shoes bound to her knees. The Wizened is a blend of their art and their imperfection. They are beautiful and perfect and broken.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I <b>would </b>very much like if your words were true and Wizened were &quot;tiny&quot; or &quot;deformed&quot; and not &quot;fairy tale cyborgs&quot;, but from what we read to this day it seems it won't be the case... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-19-2015, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T23:30:45-07:00","id":708272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708192#post708192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <b>would </b>very much like if your words were true and Wizened were &quot;tiny&quot; or &quot;deformed&quot; and not &quot;fairy tale cyborgs&quot;, but from what we read to this day it seams it wan't be the case... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple examples of 2e Wizened in the Kiths doc incorporate the imagery of their job in a fashion that evokes rather than literally incorporates the associated tools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Winter Masques</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The winter light is pale and bright<br /> And so the serpent basks,<br /> The Beast is bowed beneath the plow,<br /> The djinn rest in their flasks,<br /> <b>The craftsman\u2019s made to fit his trade,</b><br /> <b>The workers match their tasks,</b><br /> On snowy floor, we waltz the score,<br /> We masquers are our masks.<br /> \u2014 Galganvogel</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, wyrd, if you're not actually confused it would do you a world of good to stop abusing the &quot;confused&quot; emoticon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:08:27-07:00","id":708364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708272#post708272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple examples of 2e Wizened in the Kiths doc incorporate the imagery of their job in a fashion that evokes rather than literally incorporates the associated tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's about third of Wizened in Kiths doc, but the Seeming Appearance description is obvious - you are fairy tale being that changed her body for tool of her trade.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708272#post708272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, wyrd, if you're not actually confused it would do you a world of good to stop abusing the &quot;confused&quot; emoticon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know what emoticon say in HTML code, but to me it looks as &quot;displeased&quot; or &quot;grim&quot; more than &quot;confused&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:25:40-07:00","id":708395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708364#post708364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about third of Wizened in Kiths doc, but the Seeming Appearance description is obvious - you are fairy tale being that changed her body for tool of her trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>first-draft</i> description. Which is subject to change and does nothing to supersede the &quot;fairy tale being&quot; aspect of the aesthetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not know what emoticon say in HTML code, but to me it looks as &quot;displeased&quot; or &quot;grim&quot; more than &quot;confused&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the fact that your irritation does not need a tiny obnoxious waitaminute face attached, the emoticon is rerendered in quoted posts as the word &quot;confused&quot; bracketed in colons and displays the word as alt-text to anyone hovering over it.<br /> <br /> That you think it looks &quot;grim&quot; does not make it easier to take you seriously when you include it in your posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T06:59:05-07:00","id":708706,"title":"","content":"Hamster.<br /> <br /> <i>Look who you're talking to.</i><br /> <br /> There are a lot of tech-involved versions of the Wizened now, but that's a matter of the times colliding with the material, and it doesn't preclude the fact that dwarves, kobolds, and goblins are made to fit their trade biologically, and there's just as many examples of that as there are not. The Wizened-all the seemings now, really-now foster a broad icon base that better services various ideas of what a faerie is.<br /> <br /> A dwarf can be <a href=\"http://img13.deviantart.net/878b/i/2013/102/7/2/dwarven_smith_by_turnermohan-d61if00.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as much as they can be <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/16/38/7d/16387d48d1158315d71607b442a3d7b8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-19-2015, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T09:32:18-07:00","id":708867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708706#post708706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hamster.<br /> <br /> <i>Look who you're talking to.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I know that you are freelancer to the <b>Changeling</b> line - and probably playtester of 2ED. I pointed only to the info we got now and that was, till this day, approved by <b>DavidH</b> as official. Until he writes that looks of Wizened more as 1ED and &quot;fairy tale cyborgs&quot; are minority in Seeming, I will rather takes his words over yours, as it's his project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708706#post708706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of tech-involved versions of the Wizened now, but that's a matter of the times colliding with the material, and it doesn't preclude the fact that dwarves, kobolds, and goblins are made to fit their trade biologically, and there's just as many examples of that as there are not. The Wizened-all the seemings now, really-now foster a broad icon base that better services various ideas of what a faerie is.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I get it right - you say that modern Wizened are &quot;cyborgs&quot; because mortal sciences are becoming part of Arcadia stories, is that it? That Wizened <b>evolved</b> to become more suitable to the narrative of Story on the Earth? And that in past those Wizened would be still typical kobolds, dwarves, etc?<br /> <br /> If yes, I'm much more comfortable with that as &quot;transhuman story&quot; is becoming more and more of trope since times of Mary Shelley's <i>Frankenstein</i>. If in<b> Dark Eras</b> I still can make Wizened classical dwarves and kobolds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708706#post708706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dwarf can be <a href=\"http://img13.deviantart.net/878b/i/2013/102/7/2/dwarven_smith_by_turnermohan-d61if00.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as much as they can be <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/16/38/7d/16387d48d1158315d71607b442a3d7b8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you say I can populate mine Freeholds with first kind of dwarves as Wizened, I'm all ear. Because second one type looks as <i>Arcanum</i> ( video game ) - don't get me wrong, I like <i>Arcanum</i>-style from time to time. But not as main part of the basic Seeming, as their main thing distinctive from others.<br /> <br /> Or will first type dwarves need all to be Grimms from <b>Dark Eras</b>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-19-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T09:48:12-07:00","id":708877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708867#post708867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I get it right - you say that modern Wizened are &quot;cyborgs&quot; because mortal sciences are becoming part of Arcadia stories, is that it? That Wizened <b>evolved</b> to become more suitable to the narrative of Story on the Earth? And that in past those Wizened would be still typical kobolds, dwarves, etc?<br /> <br /> If yes, I'm much more comfortable with that as &quot;transhuman story&quot; is becoming more and more of trope since times of Mary Shelley's <i>Frankenstein</i>. If in<b> Dark Eras</b> I still can make Wizened classical dwarves and kobolds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a different track. If I understand Arc's meaning, the point is more that &quot;made to fit their trade&quot; is what defines the Wizened, and that this is equally applicable to individuals with more of a cyborg-like aesthetic and those more in the biological vein of kobolds, dwarves, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or will first type dwarves need all to be Grimms from <b>Dark Eras</b>? </div> </div> </div>First, no; as above, dwarves are a valid &quot;remade to suit their trade&quot; shape for a Wizened.<br /> <br /> Second, unless I've missed something, I don't think we've gotten much in the way of details or examples on the Grimm aesthetics. I'm curious to see what it turns out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Spacing tweak. 10-19-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T10:00:53-07:00","id":708883,"title":"","content":"&quot;Parts of herself are replaced with parts of her craft&quot; does not have to be so literal as to produce &quot;fairy tale cyborgs.&quot; The point is that the Wizened somehow embodies their craft.<br /> <br /> How about this for a non-cyborg example of a Wizened cellist:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); 