replace parts of their body. The tin woodsman is an obvious example. The girl with silver hands is another. The giant who had no heart in his body. Actually body modification is pretty common in fairy tales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T10:02:25-07:00","id":708885,"title":"","content":"0) My point is that between the two of us, one of us has the perspective of clarity the other one does not, and that trying to tell the one with the clearer perspective that they are wrong is a baffling bad decision.<br /> <br /> 0.1) That would be a Watsonian reading. I was speaking from a Doylist perspective. <br /> <br /> 1) What I am saying is that classical dwarves, kobolds, and goblins and other things traditionally associated with the Wizened <i>still happen with frequency today</i>. There's not a a glut of 'cyborgs' in today's world of changelings. The perception that the classic Wizened icons are somehow less in action now than they were before <i>is <b>wrong</b></i>.<br /> <br /> 2) It's not about transhumanism. It's about iconography and archetypal psychoanalytical lenses colliding with a narrative about weaving one's sense of self in opposition to the loom of reality. Some Wizened will be 'cyborgs'. Some will be classical fairy tales. It depends on the icons the character rips out of the threads for their own self within the latitude of their particular Arcadian Realm and degree of awareness.<br /> <br /> 3) Going even further from the text and simply talking about fairy tales and high fantasy and their icons in today's society, the simple fact of the matter is that there is a greater-than-ever intersection of ideas at work with the icon bases. A few examples being Artemis Fowl being a popular series with fairies that puts traditional fae alongside highly advanced sci-fi tech, Holly Black's Tithe series grunging the fuck out of the icon base, Cinder using robotics to tell a fairy tale, Hanna appropriating the theme of Little Red Riding Hood to inject some new blood into the child soldier narrative, and thousands more examples I can't even speak for. Changeling the Lost Second Edition isn't trading those out for the root icons of the classic Wizened-<i>they are still here in abundance</i>. But while it's core imagery is still built on the classics, it has broadened it's base to include the now muddier waters of images that people associate with fairy tales. It is expanding what it looks like to be a fairy tale while still leaning hard into the soul of the fairy tale.<br /> <br /> 4) I am <i>not</i> saying you can populate your freehold with mine-dwelling, gold loving, Nordic-based dwarves as Wizened. I <i>am</i> saying that Changeling the Lost Second Edition has <i>always said</i> that you can populate your freehold with mine-dwelling, gold loving, Nordic-based dwarves as Wizened. <br /> <br /> 5) You will not now or ever need Grimms to have the dwarves you grew up with. Being blunt, that's a stupid thing to think.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: This concept of the Wizened only being cyborgs in Second Editon is wrong. Stop throwing it around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T13:14:18-07:00","id":709198,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708885#post708885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;DR: This concept of the Wizened only being cyborgs in Second Editon is wrong. Stop throwing it around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad to hear this - even if mine assumption was based on two spoilers linked before. I only hope final Wizened Seeming write-up will be more direct with this point, and mentions &quot;cyborgs&quot;-like concepts in sentance or two only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708883#post708883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Parts of herself are replaced with parts of her craft&quot; does not have to be so literal as to produce &quot;fairy tale cyborgs.&quot; The point is that the Wizened somehow embodies their craft.<br /> <br /> How about this for a non-cyborg example of a Wizened cellist:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/2c/e3/0a/2ce30a64abdba6ffb738453298d1c84c.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or a Wizened bellhop:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://data.whicdn.com/images/24066713/large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they are both &quot;cyborgs&quot;. By Manfred Clynes and Nathan S. Klein, fathers of the term, in <a href=\"http://web.mit.edu/digitalapollo/Documents/Chapter1/cyborgs.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">their articular</a> the propose it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cyborgs and Space</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some of the devices necessary for creating self-regulating man-machine systems? This selfregulation must function without the benefit of consciousness in order to cooperate with the body\u2019s own autonomous homeostatic controls. For the exogenously extended organizational complex functioning as an integrated homeostatic system unconsciously, we propose the term \u201cCyborg.\u201d The Cyborg deliberately incorporates exogenous components extending the self-regulatory control function of the organism in order to adapt it to new environments.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Wizened are making tools of their trade ( exogenous components ) part of their body ( organism ) to work their Art ( self-regulatory control function ), then we get Cyborg - even if &quot;tools&quot; are violine or underwear drawer. And yes, Cyborg is correct term for this ascetics, as you see, even if there is no &quot;technology&quot; in the being itself. Enough is that &quot;tools&quot; are extension of the will of Wizened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708883#post708883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also classic fairy tale characters who do replace parts of their body. The tin woodsman is an obvious example. (...) The giant who had no heart in his body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not those two be rather Ogres, as Ogres shtick is that they loose their hearts? Tin Woodsman would be Ogre Metalflesh and Giant would be Ogre Gargantuan then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-19-2015, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T13:28:59-07:00","id":709220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=709198#post709198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, they are both &quot;cyborgs&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either this is meaningless sophistry meant to try to save face or you have been wasting everybody's time complaining about &quot;cyborgs&quot; as a facet of the Wizened focus on tradecraft that has been there since 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should not those two be rather Ogres, as Ogres shtick is that they loose their hearts? </div> </div> </div>The Ogre schtick is callusing and armoring and desensitization. <i>Every</i> seeming has something happen with their hearts; over half the seemings, Wizened included, use some variant of broken/removed/atrophied in the descriptive language surrounding the transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T15:17:22-07:00","id":709325,"title":"","content":"And reiterating, every Seeming loses their heart. It is, as it turns out, a mechanical fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T15:33:38-07:00","id":709373,"title":"","content":"One wizened I've been thinking of was a doctor before he was taken, and now he is held together by bandages like a mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T17:39:38-07:00","id":709616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=709198#post709198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, they are both &amp;quot;cyborgs&amp;quot;. By Manfred Clynes and Nathan S. Klein, fathers of the term, in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://web.mit.edu/digitalapollo/Documents/Chapter1/cyborgs.pdf&amp;quot;]their</a> articular[/URL] the propose it:<br /> <br /> If Wizened are making tools of their trade ( exogenous components ) part of their body ( organism ) to work their Art ( self-regulatory control function ), then we get Cyborg - even if &amp;quot;tools&amp;quot; are violine or underwear drawer. And yes, Cyborg is correct term for this ascetics, as you see, even if there is no &amp;quot;technology&amp;quot; in the being itself. Enough is that &amp;quot;tools&amp;quot; are extension of the will of Wizened.</div> </div> </div> </div>By this definition, Wizend were cyborgs in 1e too. Body modifications to incorporate a craft into themselves has always been Wizend's shtick, the biggest difference between 1e Wizened and 2e Wizened is just that now they make those changes to themselves, rather than their keepers making the changes to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=709198#post709198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should not those two be rather Ogres, as Ogres shtick is that they loose their hearts? Tin Woodsman would be Ogre Metalflesh and Giant would be Ogre Gargantuan then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Kith has a mention of losing their heart in the description. Well, technically it was missing from the first draft Fairest description, but it was in all of the others and we know that the lost heart is the Changeling's Icon, so presumably that will be added to the Fairest writeup in the second draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T19:36:32-07:00","id":709816,"title":"","content":"I think it's in the Fairest now too.<br /> <br /> But yeah, changelings lose their hearts and they become Icon. Better grab them before the Huntsmen do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-19-2015, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T21:03:10-07:00","id":709925,"title":"","content":"Metatangentially related: I feel like hooking that aspect of seemings into the constellation of symbols Mortality has in Promethean kicks off a fun train of thought re: the heart as an emotional regulator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T21:08:39-07:00","id":709929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=709816#post709816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's in the Fairest now too.<br /> <br /> But yeah, changelings lose their hearts and they become Icon. Better grab them before the Huntsmen do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure it is/will be in the second draft. I haven't gotten to read the second draft yet though, just redlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T09:37:52-07:00","id":712588,"title":"","content":"I feel like Goblins, Kobolds, and Dwarves are really more possible expressions of certain Kiths, rather than good examples of any one Seeming. Dwarves are supposed to be good craftsman, sure, but they have lots of other aspects and they're not necessarily defined by or obsessed with their craft. Kobolds and Goblins are generally more malicious tricksters and mischief makers than skilled, obsessive artisans. It seems as though you could make a dwarf-like or goblin-like character as almost any Seeming. They certainly <i>could</i> be Wizened, but they don't have to be. Hell, I'd say Darkling is the most obvious choice if you're going for &quot;classic&quot; Dwarfs/Goblins/Kobolds. That seems to be common in second edition when you're looking at creatures from myth/folklore/legend; there's usually more than one Seeming+Kith combination that could be used to produce a character that fits the mold. Which makes it hard to point to specific examples and say, &quot;That's an X Seeming.&quot; You pretty much have to say, &quot;That <i>could be </i> an X Seeming. It could also be othe things.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Kith examples make it pretty clear that a Wizened doesn't necessarily have to have prosthetics/implants/grafts/whathaveyou. The alterations can be more organic adaptations. That being said, literally replacing body parts or adding mechanical or artificial features in some way features heavily in both the first draft of the Seeming and the majority of the Kith examples, so it is clearly a prominent expression of the Seeming, even if it's not the only one. I would very much like to hear more examples of Fairy Tale or Fantasy characters that make for good examples of this aesthetic. The Tin Woodman and the girl with the silver hands are good examples, visually. (Even though they don't really fit the spirit of the Seeming - neither of them crafted their own replacement parts, or used representations of their art in rebuilding themselves, and neither of them were any more suited to a craft/art/trade after their transformation.) Anybody got any other good visual examples of Fantasy/Fairy characters with replacement parts or artificial add-ons? Anyone have any Fairy or Fantasy examples that fit the Wizened Seeming more closely in story as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T00:14:50-07:00","id":713828,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Rapunzel fit this image to some extend? Her long hair used as a rope fits the image somewhat... Of course, in Beauty and the Beast (at least Disney's version) we have a whole castle filled with servants looking like furniture. Mind you, I feel a bit like grasping at straws with both examples <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I vaguely recall reading about the archetype in various fairy tales, but I cannot remember any specific example...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}